IMPORT prelude

-- Accident Compensation Act 1985 (Vic) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library.
--
-- Two ways of counting days are used by the Act:
--   * plain days ("within 28 days after", "within 120 days of receiving"), counted from the day after the start;
--   * s 134AB(6A): "In calculating a period of time for the purpose of subsection (7), (10), (11), (12), (13), (14) or (16),
--     the period from 24 December to 9 January next following must be disregarded." For those periods every day from
--     24 December to 9 January is left out of the count, and a period cannot end on one of them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Accident
-- Compensation Act 1985, Version No. 237 (2 October 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published
-- with the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in
-- accordance with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Accident Compensation Act 1985`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day number of` `the day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is on or after` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `the first day` IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `falls from` `the first day` `to` `the last day` IF
        DATE_SERIAL `the day` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `the first day`
    AND DATE_SERIAL `the day` AT MOST  DATE_SERIAL `the last day`

-- The day a given number of plain days after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `plain days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

-- Plain days from one day to a later one (0 if the later day is not later).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the plain days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

§§ `s 134AB(6A) -- leaving out 24 December to 9 January`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` `falls in the Christmas period of s 134AB(6A)` IF
        (DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 12 AND DATE_DAY `the day` AT LEAST 24)
    OR  (DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 1 AND DATE_DAY `the day` AT MOST 9)

-- How many days from 24 December to 9 January fall on or before the day, counted from 1 January 1900: 17 in each whole
-- year (1-9 January and 24-31 December), plus those of the day's own year up to the day.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the left-out days up to` `the day` MEANS
    17 TIMES (DATE_YEAR `the day` MINUS 1900) PLUS `in January` PLUS `in December`
    WHERE
        `in January` MEANS
            IF DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 1
            THEN min (DATE_DAY `the day`) 9
            ELSE 9
        `in December` MEANS
            IF DATE_MONTH `the day` EQUALS 12 AND DATE_DAY `the day` AT LEAST 24
            THEN DATE_DAY `the day` MINUS 23
            ELSE 0

-- A day's place on the s 134AB(6A) count: its day number less the left-out days up to it. A left-out day has the same
-- place as the last counted day before it.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the counted day number of` `the day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day` MINUS `the left-out days up to` `the day`

-- Counted days from one day to a later one, leaving out 24 December to 9 January.
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the counted days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS `the counted day number of` `the end` MINUS `the counted day number of` `the start`

-- The last day of a period of n days after a day, leaving out 24 December to 9 January (the first counted day at least n
-- counted days after the start).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `counted days after` `the start` MEANS
    `search from` (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)
    WHERE
        GIVEN s IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A DATE
        `search from` s MEANS
            IF      (`the counted day number of` (DATE_FROM_SERIAL s) MINUS `the counted day number of` `the start`) AT LEAST n
                AND (NOT (DATE_FROM_SERIAL s) `falls in the Christmas period of s 134AB(6A)`)
            THEN DATE_FROM_SERIAL s
            ELSE `search from` (s PLUS 1)

§§ `The two years the indexed amounts are known for`

-- Division 2D of Part IV varies the amounts of the Act each 1 July from 1 July 2014 (ss 100B, 100C), and the weekly
-- payment ceilings with them. The varied amounts are not in the Act; they are published in the Victoria Government Gazette.
-- The notice deposited in subjects/au/vic/workers-compensation-annual-indexation-notice/ (Gazette S 363 of 30 June 2026)
-- prints each amount "before 1 July 2026" and "from 1 July 2026"; as in that subject's encoding, the first column is read as
-- the amount for 1 July 2025 to 30 June 2026 and the second as the amount for 1 July 2026 to 30 June 2027. Any other day
-- answers NOTHING.
DECLARE `Amounts year` IS ONE OF
    `the year from 1 July 2025`
    `the year from 1 July 2026`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Amounts year`
`the amounts year of` `the day` MEANS
    IF `the day` `falls from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2025) `to` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2026)
    THEN JUST `the year from 1 July 2025`
    ELSE IF `the day` `falls from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2026) `to` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2027)
         THEN JUST `the year from 1 July 2026`
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text: the Gazette notice for that year is not deposited)

GIVEN `the year` IS AN `Amounts year`, `before` IS A NUMBER, `from` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`in` `the year` `the amount printed` `before` `or` `from` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the year`
    WHEN `the year from 1 July 2025` THEN `before`
    WHEN `the year from 1 July 2026` THEN `from`

-- The amount for the day, or NOTHING outside the two years.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE, `before` IS A NUMBER, `from` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`on` `the day` `the amount printed` `before` `or` `from` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amounts year of` `the day`
    WHEN JUST `the year` THEN JUST (`in` `the year` `the amount printed` `before` `or` `from`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
